Context
-------
Asked whether to install anthropics/claude-plugins-official plugins/skill-creator
so guile-skills has evals, and whether process/filesystem/api-token/access
requirements belong in SKILL.md frontmatter.

What was checked, not assumed
-----------------------------
- skill-creator exists and was installed (user scope, version fa59bc903774). The
  claude-plugins-official marketplace was already configured; nothing had been
  installed before.
- Its SKILL.md says "YAML frontmatter (name, description required)" and its
  references/schemas.md is entirely eval JSON schemas -- no permission fields.
- scripts/quick_validate.py is the authority and settles it:
  ALLOWED_PROPERTIES = {name, description, license, allowed-tools, metadata,
  compatibility}; name matches ^[a-z0-9-]+$ and is <=64 chars; description
  <=1024 chars and may not contain < or >.
- All three skills validated clean before and after the change.
- Surveyed frontmatter keys across 31 installed SKILL.md files: name and
  description in all 31, then version (13), allowed-tools (8), user-invocable
  (7), tools (2), license (1), disable-model-invocation (1), argument-hint (1).
  Note that version, user-invocable, tools, disable-model-invocation and
  argument-hint are NOT in the validator's allowlist -- either newer harness
  features the bundled validator predates, or command-style fields reused. Not
  adopted here: an unvalidatable key is not worth the ambiguity.

Deviations
----------
- The user asked for "ps, fs, api/token/access requirements in the front matter".
  There is no supported field for those, so they went into metadata.requires
  (allowed by the validator) rather than new top-level keys that the loader would
  ignore. The block documents its own non-enforcement, which is the honest
  framing: it informs a reader and the model, it does not sandbox anything.
- Evals written as prompt.md + graders/*.md, not case.yaml. The CLI accepts both,
  but case.yaml carries runs/tags/max_turns/timeout_seconds/scaffold_script and
  the schema cannot be validated without early access. Guessing it risks a file
  that silently fails to parse.

Blocked
-------
`claude plugin eval` is in early access and not enabled for this account: CLI
2.1.261 answers "`plugin eval` is currently in early access" to both `eval` and
`eval init`. So the suite is authored and unscored. This is stated in
evals/README.org and in the README rather than left to be discovered, because a
plugin whose thesis is "do not claim what you did not run" cannot ship an eval
suite implied to pass. When access lands, the first run is
`claude plugin eval . --ablation with-without --allow-tools Bash`; a case that
scores the same in both arms means the skill did nothing.

